---
# Project-wide convention: variables use the fleet_ prefix (see
# ansible/group_vars/all.yml and every role's defaults), not a per-role
# prefix. ansible-lint's var-naming[no-role-prefix] rule assumes the
# opposite convention and would otherwise flag every fleet_*-named role
# default (e.g. fleet_network_hardening_enabled, fleet_ufw_ssh_port) as a
# violation. Internal role-scratch vars (nh_*, register: results) are
# exempt for the same reason — they follow the same project-wide style of
# short, role-scoped-by-context prefixes rather than the full role name.
skip_list:
  - var-naming[no-role-prefix]
